## 📈 Model Performance

| Model | ROC AUC | F1 Score | Recall | CV AUC (5-fold) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Gradient Boosting** | **0.843** | **0.621** | **0.587** | **0.839 ± 0.011** |
| Random Forest | 0.812 | 0.598 | 0.561 | 0.808 ± 0.014 |
| Logistic Regression | 0.781 | 0.571 | 0.534 | 0.778 ± 0.016 |

**Why Recall matters most here:**
Missing a churner (false negative) = losing a customer with no chance to retain them.
A false alarm (wrong churn prediction) = offering a discount unnecessarily — cheap mistake.
Recall is the metric that minimises the expensive error.

