## 🔑 Key Design Decisions

**Why Pipeline (scaler + model together)?**
StandardScaler must apply the exact same transformation at training and serving time. Packaging them together as a Pipeline ensures this automatically. Scaling separately is the most common ML serving bug.

**Why 5-fold StratifiedKFold CV?**
Churn rate is ~26% — imbalanced. Without stratification, some folds might have very different churn rates, giving misleading CV scores. Stratified ensures each fold has the same distribution.

**Why PSI alongside KS test?**
KS test detects shape changes in distributions. PSI detects proportion shifts between buckets. They catch different types of drift. Using both catches more real-world drift patterns than either alone.

